# Ticket State Machine (CRITICAL)

## Statuses
Open, In Progress, Resolved, Closed, Cancelled

## Allowed Transitions (ONLY these)
- Open          -> In Progress
- In Progress   -> Resolved
- Resolved      -> Closed
- Open          -> Cancelled
- In Progress   -> Cancelled

## Enforcement Rules
- ALL other transitions MUST be rejected (e.g., Resolved->Open, Closed->anything,
  Cancelled->anything, Open->Resolved, skipping states)
- Enforce in a DEDICATED class: com.mysite.core.statemachine.TicketStateMachine
  (or TransitionValidator) — NEVER scatter transition logic across servlets
- On invalid transition: throw com.mysite.core.exception.InvalidTransitionException
  which the servlet maps to HTTP 409 Conflict with a clear JSON error message
- Initial status on ticket creation is always "Open"

## Testing Requirement
- Every VALID transition must have a passing test
- Representative INVALID transitions must have a test proving rejection
- Name tests clearly, e.g., shouldRejectResolvedToOpenTransition()
